        {
          "exampleId": "w:sound#e-4aed08d8c2f697b1",
          "text": "More than 30 years ago, the scholar Charles Hockett noted that speech sounds called labiodentals, such as “f” and “v”, were more common in the languages of societies that ate softer foods.",
