        },
        {
          "exampleId": "w:sound#e-3f4e7d8c93bf42bd",
          "text": "“The set of speech sounds we use has not necessarily remained stable since the appearance of human beings, but rather the huge variety of speech sounds that we find today is the product of a complex interplay of things like biological change and cultural evolution,” said Steven Moran, a member of the research team.",
